- Measured live (docs/knowledge/apply-latency.md): mailbox transaction 1 ms median; 194 ms median between transactions; real audit log 15.9 MB. Your bench must reproduce the overhead shape on a synthetic 16 MB log first (report per-part timing: read_state parse, lock, audit fsync, health snapshots, pacer), THEN optimize the biggest parts.
- This is security-relevant code (guard). Semantics must be identical; an Opus reviewer will read your diff adversarially. Prefer small, obviously-correct changes with tests over cleverness. Document each change's invariant in the code comment and in your report.
- Keep: one transaction at a time, health snapshot before and after every transaction, fsync of the attempt record before the write, read-back, budget/dwell checks semantics, fail-closed on any unreadable state.
